nerated":true,"title":"Type Aliases"},{"anchor":"Enumerations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BoundedResponse","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/FlushOutcome"],"generated":true,"title":"Enumerations"},{"anchor":"Extended-Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Foundation"],"generated":true,"title":"Extended Modules"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"Swidux-logo"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux is a Redux-style state-management library for SwiftUI. State lives in one observable store, mutations go through reducers, and side effects run as async effects. Macros generate the observability boilerplate. Built-in plugins handle persistence and undo\/redo. Optional plugins ship ready-made paywalls (RevenueCat or StoreKit-shaped), version killswitches, parental gates, analytics (Mixpanel or any backend), feature flags, and SwiftData\/iCloud persistence."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The dispatch cycle:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["View → store.send(.action)","  → willReduce hooks (UndoPlugin snapshots here)","  → reducer mutates state in place, optionally returns Effect","  → plugin reducers handle their own actions","  → afterReduce hooks (PersistencePlugin drains EntityStore changelogs here)","  → observer tree updates only changed properties (per-property observation)","  → effects run on a background actor; results dispatch back via @MainActor send"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Your domain types and database stay in your app. Swidux provides the contracts, observability, and dispatch loop."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Companion Packages","type":"heading","anchor":"Companion-Packages"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vendor-specific adapters live in their